  "question": {
    "text": "An equilateral triangle is made by uniform wires $A B, B C, C A .$ A current $I$ enters at $A$ and leaves from the mid point of $B C$. If the lengths of each side of the triangle is $L,$ the magnetic field $B$ at the centroid $O$ of the triangle is <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2013_phy_q22.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sKoHl",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_{0}}{4 \\pi}\\left(\\frac{4 L}{L}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Urokp",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_{0}}{2 \\pi}\\left(\\frac{4 L}{L}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mcJj3",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_{0}}{4 \\pi}\\left(\\frac{2 L}{L}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0WYwb",
      "text": "zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The given situation can be shown as\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2013_phy_a22.png\">\r\n\r\nThe magnetic field at centroid $O$ = Magnetic field due to left part + Magnetic field due to right part\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$$\r\n\\mathrm{B}=\\mathrm{B}_{1}+\\mathrm{B}_{2}=0\r\n$$\r\n(: direction of $B$ due to both parts is different of $O$ )",
    "image": null
